From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:26:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg/FmpDeviceSmmLib: Only the regions the platform
 allows

[ouroBIOS: patches/edk2/0045, without the files that TianoCore's tree
does not have (tools/edk2-import.py): 10 in edk2/OuroBiosPkg (8 in a
directory of TianoCore's that the package carries whole)]

The library writes every region that the manifest of a signed capsule
names, through the SMMSTORE handler, which serves the whole flash on a
boot with update capsules: a capsule built wrong, naming the variable
store, the vital product data or the GbE region of the descriptor, is
written as it says. And on a flash with the two RW slots of vboot only
a manifest with both is written one slot at a time: one with a slot
alone writes that slot whether it runs or not, and leaves vboot nothing
to fall back to.

Add PcdFmpDeviceSmmAllowedRegions, the names of the regions that an
update may write: the image check, and the write before it writes
anything, refuse a manifest with another region, with
LAST_ATTEMPT_STATUS_SMMSTORE_INVALID_IMAGE. A list without names, the
default, allows every region, as before. The platform allows the two
slots and RW_MRC_CACHE, the regions of the capsules of ouroBIOS. A
flash with both slots takes only a manifest with both, or refuses the
image the same way. The Firmware Update page of the setup names that
status for all it covers now: an invalid image or region manifest.

FmpDeviceSmmManifest.h includes UefiBaseType.h for EFI_STATUS, so that
FmpDeviceSmmVboot.c builds in the host unit test too.

TEST=The host unit tests (UefiPayloadPkg/Test/UefiPayloadPkgHostTest.dsc),
19 of 19, on the host and in the CI of ouroBIOS: the regions of the
release capsules allowed in any order; SMMSTORE, SI_GBE, a prefix or a
longer name refused; a list without names allowing every region; a
flash with both slots taking only a manifest with both.
tools/qemu-update.py of ouroBIOS: a capsule naming SMMSTORE next to the
slots, and one with the running slot alone, are refused with nothing
written (QEMU's trace of the flash), 0x1800 in the ESRT; the release
capsules are written as before.
---
diff --git a/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dec b/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dec
index 574d105..bdaf58d 100644
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dec
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dec
@@ -188,3 +188,9 @@ gUefiPayloadPkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdCfrSetupMenuPasswordCategory|L"Security"|VOID*|
 #  graphical UI, to those of them that are there. An empty string leaves
 #  them out.
 gUefiPayloadPkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdCfrSetupMenuGeneralCategory|L"General"|VOID*|0x00000031
+
+## The FMAP regions that an update capsule may write (FmpDeviceSmmLib), their
+#  names separated by spaces: a capsule whose manifest names another region
+#  is refused before anything is written.  A list without names allows
+#  every region of the flash map.
+gUefiPayloadPkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdFmpDeviceSmmAllowedRegions|""|VOID*|0x00000032
-- 
